<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tirukkural</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kural, Thirukkural</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tirukkural is a classic Tamil work of 1,330 couplets on ethics, attributed to the poet Thiruvalluvar. Divided into three books on virtue, wealth and love, it gives practical guidance on personal conduct, kingship and household life. Its date is debated, with many scholars placing it around the 5th century CE, and it is among the most widely read and translated works of Indian literature.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tirukkural.jpg" alt="Tirukkural" width="320" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: பேரா. சுந்தரசண்முகனார் · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%AE%A4%E0%AE%BF%E0%AE%B0%E0%AF%81%E0%AE%95%E0%AF%8D%E0%AE%95%E0%AF%81%E0%AE%B1%E0%AE%B3%E0%AF%8D_%E0%AE%A4%E0%AF%86%E0%AE%B3%E0%AE%BF%E0%AE%B5%E0%AF%81.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
